<MarketArticleLayout
  title="Private Label Activewear Manufacturer for UK Brands"
  description="A practical guide for UK activewear buyers comparing ready-stock styles, private label branding and OEM development with a China-based supplier."
  market="United Kingdom"
  readTime="6 min read"
  tags={['UK', 'Private Label', 'Gym Wear', 'Sourcing']}
>
  <p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Fitclo is a China-based activewear supplier serving UK buyers. A UK brand can start with an existing style, discuss private label branding for a selected product, or bring a defined brief for OEM/ODM development. These are different sourcing routes; current colours, sizes, sample options, branding feasibility, order quantity and shipping scope need confirmation for the chosen product. This is not a UK manufacturing offer.</p>

  <h2>Which Sourcing Route Fits Your UK Brand?</h2>
  <p>Choose the route before comparing quotations. A product image alone does not establish that a particular colour, size mix or logo method is available for your order.</p>
  <div class="market-table">
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Route</th><th>Start With</th><th>Confirm Before Ordering</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td><a href="/ready-to-ship/">Ready-stock styles</a></td><td>A listed style number, preferred colour and size mix.</td><td>Current availability, sample option and shipment scope.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/private-label/">Private label</a></td><td>A selected product plus logo, label and packaging brief.</td><td>Which branding methods are feasible on that style and what the approved sample will show.</td></tr>
        <tr><td><a href="/oem-activewear-manufacturer/">OEM/ODM development</a></td><td>A tech pack, reference sample or detailed product brief.</td><td>Fabric, fit, construction, sample revisions and production requirements.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2>Product Starting Points for a UK Activewear Collection</h2>
  <p>Browse the current <a href="/products/sports-bras/">sports bra</a>, <a href="/products/leggings/">leggings</a> and <a href="/products/matching-sets/">matching-set</a> references. If you already have a product direction, use the <a href="/private-label-sports-bras/">sports bra</a> or <a href="/private-label-leggings/">leggings</a> buyer brief to specify fit, fabric, size range and branding. Ask Fitclo to confirm the order route for the exact styles you choose.</p>

  <h2>What UK Brands Should Prioritise</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Specify the intended customer and size range; check garment measurements and fit samples rather than relying on an image.</li>
    <li>For leggings, define coverage and stretch-recovery checks. For sports bras, state the activity and support intent before assessing a sample.</li>
    <li>Agree on artwork, label content and packaging requirements before approving branding.</li>
    <li>Record the approved sample, inspection priorities and shipment terms for the actual order.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What to Send for a Useful UK Sourcing Reply</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Product type or style number, intended activity and destination in the UK.</li>
    <li>Target quantity, preferred colours, sizes and required launch timing.</li>
    <li>Logo artwork, label and packaging needs, plus whether you require a sample.</li>
    <li>Any tech pack, reference images or fit issues that the supplier should address.</li>
  </ul>

  <p>Use the <a href="/wholesale-to/united-kingdom/">UK activewear sourcing page</a> to compare the three routes and request a response for your selected products. Confirm the final specification, commercial terms and logistics for your order before committing to a launch date.</p>
</MarketArticleLayout>
